{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788385829492,"sessionID":"ses_f9be5f3dcffewQilm2OnCwwf8H","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a5775bd357c41559","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Book Collection REST API\n2: \n3: A small REST API for managing a book collection, built with TypeScript, Express, and SQLite (via `better-sqlite3`).\n4: \n5: ## Endpoints\n6: \n7: | Method | Path             | Description                          |\n8: |--------|------------------|--------------------------------------|\n9: | GET    | `/health`        | Health check                         |\n10: | POST   | `/books`         | Create a new book                    |\n11: | GET    | `/books`         | List all books (supports `?author=`) |\n12: | GET    | `/books/{id}`    | Get a single book                    |\n13: | PUT    | `/books/{id}`    | Update a book                        |\n14: | DELETE | `/books/{id}`    | Delete a book                        |\n15: \n16: ### Book fields\n17: - `title` (string, **required**)\n18: - `author` (string, **required**)\n19: - `year` (integer, optional)\n20: - `isbn` (string, optional)\n21: \n22: ### Status codes\n23: - `200` – successful read / update\n24: - `201` – created\n25: - `204` – deleted\n26: - `400` – validation error\n27: - `404` – book not found\n28: \n29: ## Setup\n30: \n31: ```bash\n32: npm install\n33: npm run build\n34: ```\n35: \n36: ## Run\n37: \n38: ```bash\n39: npm start\n40: # or run directly from source:\n41: npm run dev\n42: ```\n43: \n44: By default the server listens on `http://localhost:3000` and persists data to `books.db`. Override via environment variables:\n45: \n46: ```bash\n47: PORT=4000 DB_PATH=/tmp/books.db npm start\n48: ```\n49: \n50: For an in-memory database (e.g. for quick experiments):\n51: \n52: ```bash\n53: DB_PATH=:memory: npm start\n54: ```\n55: \n56: ## Tests\n57: \n58: ```bash\n59: npm test\n60: ```\n61: \n62: Tests use Mocha + Chai + Supertest. They run against an in-memory SQLite database and cover both the HTTP API and the data store directly.\n63: \n64: ## Example\n65: \n66: ```bash\n67: curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/books \\\n68:   -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n69:   -d '{\"title\":\"Dune\",\"author\":\"Frank Herbert\",\"year\":1965,\"isbn\":\"9780441172719\"}'\n70: \n71: curl http://localhost:3000/books?author=Frank%20Herbert\n72: ```\n\n(End of file - total 72 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Book Collection REST API\n\nA small REST API for managing a book collection, built with TypeScript, Express, and SQLite (via `better-sqlite3`).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n| Method | Path             | Description                          |\n|--------|------------------|--------------------------------------|\n| GET    | `/health`        | Health check                         |\n| POST   | `/books`         | Create a new book                    |\n| GET    | `/books`         | List all books (supports `?author=`) |\n| GET    | `/books/{id}`    | Get a single book                    |\n| PUT    | `/books/{id}`    | Update a book                        |\n| DELETE | `/books/{id}`    | Delete a book                        |\n\n### Book fields\n- `title` (string, **required**)\n- `author` (string, **required**)\n- `year` (integer, optional)\n- `isbn` (string, optional)","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/README.md","text":"# Book Collection REST API\n\nA small REST API for managing a book collection, built with TypeScript, Express, and SQLite (via `better-sqlite3`).\n\n## Endpoints\n\n| Method | Path             | Description                          |\n|--------|------------------|--------------------------------------|\n| GET    | `/health`        | Health check                         |\n| POST   | `/books`         | Create a new book                    |\n| GET    | `/books`         | List all books (supports `?author=`) |\n| GET    | `/books/{id}`    | Get a single book                    |\n| PUT    | `/books/{id}`    | Update a book                        |\n| DELETE | `/books/{id}`    | Delete a book                        |\n\n### Book fields\n- `title` (string, **required**)\n- `author` (string, **required**)\n- `year` (integer, optional)\n- `isbn` (string, optional)\n\n### Status codes\n- `200` – successful read / update\n- `201` – created\n- `204` – deleted\n- `400` – validation error\n- `404` – book not found\n\n## Setup\n\n```bash\nnpm install\nnpm run build\n```\n\n## Run\n\n```bash\nnpm start\n# or run directly from source:\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nBy default the server listens on `http://localhost:3000` and persists data to `books.db`. Override via environment variables:\n\n```bash\nPORT=4000 DB_PATH=/tmp/books.db npm start\n```\n\nFor an in-memory database (e.g. for quick experiments):\n\n```bash\nDB_PATH=:memory: npm start\n```\n\n## Tests\n\n```bash\nnpm test\n```\n\nTests use Mocha + Chai + Supertest. They run against an in-memory SQLite database and cover both the HTTP API and the data store directly.\n\n## Example\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:3000/books \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"title\":\"Dune\",\"author\":\"Frank Herbert\",\"year\":1965,\"isbn\":\"9780441172719\"}'\n\ncurl http://localhost:3000/books?author=Frank%20Herbert\n```","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":72,"totalLines":72,"truncated":false}},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1788385829481,"end":1788385829489}},"id":"prt_0641a222c001VZaJMEtk0LwfSb","sessionID":"ses_f9be5f3dcffewQilm2OnCwwf8H","messageID":"msg_0641a1e0f001XemQ4lKDcBgUI3"}}
